jobs.description:
As an Order Planner, you are the key link between customers, production, purchasing, customer service, and our external production partners. You ensure that orders are processed correctly, schedules are accurate, and delivery commitments are met.

What will you do?

- Process and review customer orders.
- Coordinate and confirm delivery dates.
- Prepare and maintain production and delivery schedules.
- Adjust schedules in response to changes in demand, capacity, or material availability.
- Communicate daily with production, purchasing, customer service, and external partners.
- Monitor orders and deliveries and make adjustments where necessary.

This position is available on both a part-time and full-time basis. You will work regular daytime hours, from 8:30 AM to 5:00 PM.

- MBO-level education and working experience;
- Experience in order planning is a plus, but not a requirement;
- Experience with ERP systems (e.g. Navision) and proficient in using Excel;
- Accurate, well-organized, and strong communication skills;
- A practical mindset and the ability to maintain an overview in a dynamic environment;
- Good command of English.

As a warehouse operator, you’re the key player in the logistics process. You unload trucks and containers, stack goods on pallets, and make sure everything is scanned, labeled, and shrink-wrapped correctly. You use internal transport equipment like forklifts and reach trucks to move everything quickly and safely. You count inventory, pick orders, and get them ready for shipping. You also help with value-added activities like packaging or labeling products. You’ll work full time (40 hours a week), mostly in day shifts. Together with your colleagues, you keep the warehouse tidy and safe. You work closely with your team leader and supervisor, and your day flies by thanks to the variety of tasks. Speed, accuracy, and safety are always at the heart of your job as a warehouse operator.

This is what we ask from you:

- You are at least 18 years old and have a VMBO level of education or equivalent working and thinking level;
- You have a good command of the English language;
- You enjoy working as part of a team;
- You live within commuting distance of Moerdijk and have your own transportation;
